
*** Service Deployment ****
The AWS instance consists of the following services: Mosquitto MQTT, InfluxDB, Node-RED and Home Assistant. 
This file presents the necessary steps for the installation of such services.

- Requirements: SSH access to the instance (Use Putty)

---- Mosquitto MQTT Broker ----

* Mosquitto Broker and Mosquitto Clients Installation 
sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y
sudo apt install mosquitto mosquitto-clients 

* Create a password file and add users:
sudo mosquitto_passwd -c /etc/mosquitto/passwd <user_name>
sudo chown mosquitto:mosquitto /etc/mosquitto/passwd 
sudo chmod 640 /etc/mosquitto/passwd

* Broker Configuration TLS 
nano /etc/mosquitto/config/mosquitto.conf
- Add following:
listener 8883
allow_anonymous false
password_file /etc/mosquitto/passwd

---- InfluxDB Dababase ----

* Download the InfluxData repository key
sudo wget -q https://repos.influxdata.com/influxdata-archive_compat.key

* Verify the key and install it:
sudo echo '393e8779c89ac8d958f81f942f9ad7fb82a25e133faddaf92e15b16e6ac9ce4c influxdata-archive_compat.key' | sha256sum -c && cat influxdata-archive_compat.key | gpg --dearmor | sudo tee /etc/apt/trusted.gpg.d/influxdata-archive_compat.gpg > /dev/null

* Add the InfluxData repository:
sudo echo 'deb [signed-by=/etc/apt/trusted.gpg.d/influxdata-archive_compat.gpg] https://repos.influxdata.com/debian stable main' | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/influxdata.list

* Update package lists and install InfluxDB:
sudo sudo apt-get update && sudo apt-get install influxdb

* Start and Enable InfluxDB Service

sudo sudo service influxdb start
systemctl unmask influxdb
systemctl enable influxdb
systemctl start influxdb
systemctl status influxdb

---- NodeRED ----

* Install curl (required for NVM installation):
sudo apt install curl -y

* Install NVM (Node Version Manager):
curl https://raw.githubusercontent.com/creationix/nvm/master/install.sh | bash
source ~/.bashrc

* Install Node.js (16.14.0 is required)
nvm install 16.14.0
node -v

* Install npm
sudo apt-get install npm -y
npm -v

* Install Node-RED and Node-RED Admin globally:
sudo npm install -g --unsafe-perm node-red node-red-admin

